# Episode 01 – Meeting Request Form Setup

The goal of this episode was to create a simple and professional way for potential clients to request a meeting without needing to send emails manually.

Before building this workflow, a client would usually contact me through email, social media, or chat. Managing those requests manually can become difficult as the number of inquiries grows. Important details are often scattered across different platforms, making it harder to keep everything organized.

To solve this problem, I created a Google Form that acts as a centralized meeting request system.

The form collects all the information required before a consultation call, including the client's name, email address, company name, preferred meeting date, preferred time, meeting type, and project details.

Every form submission is automatically stored inside Google Sheets. This sheet becomes the single source of truth for the entire automation workflow.

By collecting structured information at the beginning, the workflow becomes more reliable and scalable. It also improves the client experience because clients can submit everything they need in one place instead of exchanging multiple messages.

At the end of this episode, I had a working meeting request form connected directly to Google Sheets, ready to trigger future automation steps.
